    <record>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-158-secure-inherit-filed-records.md (rule, inventory, live counts, triggers, sharees, unsecure, interpretations i-xii, placement and three-question table, tests, seeds, live gates, owner questions, handovers, merge points)</record>
    <summary>
      (1) Rule: a sprk_workassignment or sprk_project FILED UNDER a sprk_matter / sprk_project with sprk_issecure = true (a work assignment's typed sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingproject; the pair sprk_regardingrecordid + sprk_regardingrecordtype on either, whose TYPE decides) is made a real secure root - flagged, the named Secure Record Owners team, its own container, its recorded creator shared - through ProvisionProjectEndpoint's own steps (new entry ProvisionInheritedAsync: the endpoint core with ProvisioningCreator.RecordedCreator, createdby else sprk_createdbyperson; Step 4.1 sets the flag first, task 150's EnsureSecureFlagAsync verbatim). One owner: Services/Access/SecureRootInheritance (secure-if-any; an unreadable or EMPTY parent flag is never "not secure": with no other secure parent nothing is written / the write is refused, beside a readable secure parent the record is secured and its sharees held).
      (2) Create and re-file: SecureRootFilingGate (singleton) - CheckAsync before the write (refuses record_owner_parent_undetermined, nothing written) and SecureAfterWriteAsync after it - wired into dataverse.create_record (created as an ordinary row of the caller's unit, then provisioned: S5), dataverse.update_record, DataverseUpdateHandler, UpdateRecordActionCore, the field-mapping push and the Office project quick-create. A host without the inheritance refuses a filing write. POST /api/v1/work-assignments is not wired (task 166 deletes it; it cannot file under a matter).
      (3) Transition: provisioning Step 8 (after 148's child pass) secures every work assignment / project filed under the record, recursively (bound 3, deeper left to the job); incomplete = the existing 500 sdap.provision.children_incomplete with filedRecords; the 200 carries filedRecords; the already-provisioned call completes it.
      (4) Job: SecureRootInheritanceJob (IScheduledJob, every 5 minutes, writes on, at most 25 provisionings per run; failed scan = failed run; incomplete record = Success false).
      (5) Sharees: SecureChildShareSynchronizer.SyncInheritedRootAsync - task 149's mirror (intersection, No Access guard, not-isolated parent holds), ADD-ONLY on a root; passed on inline by /share-user and by a project that was just given sharees (SecureRootInheritance.PassSharesOnAsync, never provisions).
      (6) Unsecure: never auto-unsecure; relatedSecureRecords listed; optional alsoUnsecure checked per record by F3 (task 146-c1's SecureDesignationRemoval, copied byte-identical); a record whose parent is still secure is refused 409 sdap.unsecure.parent_still_secure naming the parent; unreadable parent 500 sdap.unsecure.parent_unverifiable.
    </summary>
    <escalations>The POML trigger did NOT fire: the job reads data, not the writing path, so no write outside the BFF can hide a filed record from it for more than one 5-minute run. Owner / main-session questions recorded (note section 11), the work complete under the stated interpretations: Q1 - a parent UNSHARE is not propagated to filed records (add-only; a root's mirrored and own shares cannot be told apart) - ANSWERED by round 30 (provenance, option (c); implemented in fix round r1); Q2 - section 6.5 path B extension for the user-OBO update tool's inline securing - ACCEPTED by owner round 32 (Amendment A-UAC158; no longer PROPOSED). Interpretations recorded owner-reversible: still-secure-parent refusal (POML), matter/project parents only, create-then-provision (S5 - superseded by round 31 item 2 in r1: created INTO isolation), secure-if-any with an unreadable sibling (revised by round 31 item 1 in r1: refused).</escalations>
    <step-9-5>
      <code-review>Self-review over every changed file; fixed during the task: (a) an uninterpretable filing value escaped CheckRefileAsync as an exception (now a refusal; seed S24); (b) the parent decision returned "unknown" as soon as any parent was unreadable, leaving a record under a readably secure parent unsecured - fail OPEN (now secure-if-any, sharees held; S04/S05); (c) the filed-roots listing matched a pair by id only, so the unsecure response could offer an unrelated record (now type-exact, unconfirmed candidates excluded; S06/S07); (d) a work assignment secured inside a project's provisioning missed the matter's sharees until the job (now passed on in the same call; S39); (e) a parent's new sharee waited for the job (now /share-user passes it on; S38); (f) a create re-read its row after writing it even when filed under nothing - the full-host Office contract tests warned (now the create passes its own columns; S42/S43); (g) misleading chat error copy ("not shared beyond its team" for a BU-visible row) corrected; stale "a root under a secure parent is refused" remarks updated. (h) NetArchTest census: the unsecure owner write moved into UnsecureRecordAsync (entry renamed) and the 156 x 146 merge artifact in IncomingAssociationResolver (an in-memory row read as a create) fixed as integ/uac-r2-batch4 does. Open, owner questions: Q1, Q2. Known residuals recorded in the note and the I-11 registry row: a created record is BU-visible between its create and the owner move (same call; on failure until the job), a parent's unshare is not propagated, provisioning a parent with many filed records runs one provisioning each in that request.</code-review>
      <adr-check>ADR-002 no plugins (WP-1 one owner SecureRootInheritance; WP-5 the job) compliant. ADR-003 fail closed compliant (unknown parent never "not secure", refusals before any write, failed scan = failed run, incomplete = error/warning/Success false, never reported as success). ADR-010 concrete classes, no new interface. ADR-013: AI handlers / nodes call Services.Access, never the reverse. ADR-032 every registration unconditional (gate beside the restamper in AddCoreAncestorResolver; inheritance + job in ExternalAccessModule). ADR-036 A1: AddScheduledJob, idempotent per record, throw on an incomplete scan, heartbeat per attempt, no scheduler-store dependency. ADR-038: tests on KEEP paths (tests/integration/data-mutation), real routes driven, boundary mocks only, no banned pattern; every guard seeded. ADR-052: BFF IScheduledJob. ADR-028: no new endpoint or auth surface; /share-user and /unsecure-project keep their authorization; app-only provisioning runs only after the caller's own checked write. Section 6.5: path B extension PROPOSED (Q2) - surfaced, not silent.</adr-check>
